<h1> Why Are STEM Programs Important?</h1>

<img src="image/gears1.png">

<h2>What Is STEM?</h2>
    <p>STEM stands for science, technology, engineering, and math. It is also sometimes refered to as STEAM where the 'A' represents Arts. STEM is a combination of all these key concepts.</p>

<h2>Why is STEM Important?</h2>
    <p>Science, math, engineering, and technology are what buildour tomorrow. Without any STEM subjects modern day society would be no where. There would be no inovation, no new creative ideas, there would be nothing. At least not anything as it is known today. Picture a world without even the simplist of technology or tools, or heaven forbid a world without cell phones! The horror! It is truth though. Without STEM subjects the world can kiss its cars, computers, buildings, and understanding of science goodbye. So if you are thinking "Why should I care about math?" or "Science is pointless, why do I have to learn it in school?" just take a look around.</p>

<h2>What Skills Does STEM Foster?</h2>

<h3>Problem Sovling and Critical Thinking</h3>
    <p>Not only would having STEM programs benefit students generally in math, science, technology and engineering but it would also help build problem solving and critical thinking skills. These essential skills allow students to work outside of the box to solve new problems by  putting all the knowledge they have together, or in other words applying everything they've learned. Critical thinking is an essential and versatile life skill that can be used in almost any professional field along with many everyday experiences.</p>

<h3>Creatvity</h3>
    <p>Creativity goes hand in hand with critical thinking. It allows students to create new and interesting solutions to problems. By allowing students creative freedom in areas like engineering and technology it fosters a lot of creative thinking. The use of creativity in STEM is also why it is sometimes referred to as STEAM, with the 'A' standing for arts.</p>

<h2>Results of Inaccissible STEM Programs</h2>

<h3>Prevention of Innovation</h3>
    <p>STEM programs create the innovators of tomorrow. Without people in STEM and/or STEAM the world will never be able to grow change and thrive. </p>

<h3>Math In Canada Over The Past Few Years</h3>
    <p>Students' math scores have been declining over the past few years and the trend hasn't stopped. The averages in math have dropped. In the year 2023 only 59% of grade 3's were at the provincial standard, 47% of grade 6's and 52% of grade 9's. With the EQAO test approaching, those numbers are almost sure to be even lower this year. One of the reasons for this drop is in fact lack of accessible STEM programs. Less students are able to get help in areas like math and without that help less students are able to succeed. Again referring back to 2023, only 12% were considered high achievers. With more programs that help students with math and other subjects this 12% has the potential to be much higher.</p>

